      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-182340",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to prove the following statement using mathematical induction:\n\n> $n! > 2^{n}$ for all $n \\ge 4, n \u2208 N$\n\nA proof template is outlined below. Fill in the missing statements.\n\n**Base Case**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base case {{field-1}}.\n\n$1$! {{field-2}} {{field-3}}\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that for some $n =$\n{{field-4}},\nwe have\n\n$2$ {{field-5}} {{field-6}}\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$(k + 1)$! {{field-7}} {{field-8}}\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, $n! > 2^{n}$ for all $n \\ge 4$."
    },
